8. Comparison with Known Results

8.1. Caffarelli–Kohn–Nirenberg partial regularity

The CKN theorem gives that the one-dimensional parabolic Hausdorff measure of the singular set is zero. The maximal non-concentration condition (5.3) can be viewed as a quantitative strengthening of this statement: not only is the singular set small, but the local enstrophy maximal function is controlled except possibly on a set of small measure.

8.2. Escauriaza–Seregin–Šverák and Prodi–Serrin criteria

These criteria are subcritical and unconditional. The present framework operates at the critical level, where the corresponding questions are open. The scaling gap between the subcritical L^p_t L^q_x conditions and the critical Carleson geometry is exactly the gap between the known unconditional regularity theory and the conditional program proposed here.

