10. Axisymmetric Program

In the no-swirl axisymmetric case, the standard bound on \Gamma=\omega^\phi/r remains the key structural input. The following concrete target is added.

Target 10.1. Derive a local version of the \Gamma bound on dyadic cylinders Q^* centered on the symmetry axis:

\sup_{Q^*\subset \text{axis neighborhood}}
\left(
\frac{1}{|Q|}\int_{Q^*} |\Gamma|^2
\right)^{1/2}
\le
C(\Gamma_0,\mathrm{geometry}).
\tag{10.1}

If such a local bound holds, then the dyadic Carleson bilinear conjecture (5.1) may be verified in the no-swirl axisymmetric class, providing the first unconditional confirmation of the framework in a nontrivial setting.

For flows with swirl, Conjecture 10.3 of Version 4.1 is retained: bounded vorticity direction gradient implies regularity. This can be approached through the same dyadic Carleson program.

