Appendix G. Axisymmetric Program: Local \Gamma Bound

We outline a possible derivation of a local bound on \Gamma=\omega^\phi/r in the no-swirl axisymmetric case.

G.1. Global bound

In the no-swirl case, \Gamma satisfies

(\partial_t+u\cdot\nabla-\Delta)\Gamma
=
-\frac{2}{r}\partial_r\Gamma.

The maximum principle gives

\|\Gamma(t)\|_{L^\infty}
\le
\|\Gamma_0\|_{L^\infty}.
\tag{G.1}

G.2. Local version

Let Q be a dyadic cube of side length R=2^{-j} centered on the symmetry axis. We seek

\left(
\frac{1}{|Q|}
\int_{Q^*}
|\Gamma(s,y)|^2\,dy\,ds
\right)^{1/2}
\le
C(\Gamma_0,\mathrm{geometry}).
\tag{G.2}

Approach. Use the local energy inequality for \Gamma on Q^*. The damping term -2\partial_r\Gamma/r is negative in the radial direction, which may provide extra decay. However, the nonlocal nature of the pressure and the axisymmetric geometry introduce technical complications.

Status. The derivation of (G.2) is work in progress. If successful, it would provide the first unconditional verification of Conjecture 5.1 in a nontrivial special case.

